    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a person sends a document or information by post if he posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information"

-- src:19403 | 3 (1) A document or information in hard copy form may be sent or supplied by hand or by post to an address (in accordance with paragraph 4).
@ref sch 4 para 3(1) Method of communication in hard copy form (src:19403)
GIVEN `the means of sending or supplying` IS A `sch 4 means of sending or supplying`
      `the person posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 3(1) the means is one by which hard copy may be sent or supplied` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the means of sending or supplying`
    WHEN `sch 4 by hand` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `sch 4 by post` THEN
        CONSIDER `sch 4 para 3(2) the person sends the document or information by post` `the person posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information`
        WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by post" is, for this Schedule, posting a prepaid envelope (para 3(2)); a posting without one is outside the grant
    WHEN `sch 4 by electronic means` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be sent or supplied by hand or by post"
    WHEN `sch 4 by some other means` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may be sent or supplied by hand or by post"

-- src:19406 | 4 A document or information in hard copy form may be sent or supplied—
-- src:19407 | (a) to an address specified by the company for the purpose;
-- src:19408 | (b) to the company's registered office;
-- src:19409 | (c) to an address to which any provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied.
