GIVEN `the address is specified by the company for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 86 the company has its registered office at the address` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied to the address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 4 the address is one to which hard copy may be sent or supplied` MEANS
    IF       `the address is specified by the company for the purpose`
         OR  `s 86 the company has its registered office at the address` EQUALS JUST TRUE
         OR  `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied to the address`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "may be sent or supplied— (a) to an address specified by the company for the purpose; (b) to the company's registered office; (c) to an address to which any provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied"

-- src:19401 | 2 A document or information is validly sent or supplied to a company if it is sent or supplied in hard copy form in accordance with this Part of this Schedule.
@ref sch 4 para 2 Validly sent in hard copy form (src:19401)
GIVEN `the form of the document or information` IS A `sch 4 form of the document or information`
      `the means of sending or supplying` IS A `sch 4 means of sending or supplying`
      `the person posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address is specified by the company for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 86 the company has its registered office at the address` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied to the address` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 para 2 the document or information is validly sent or supplied in hard copy form` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the form of the document or information`
    WHEN `sch 4 hard copy form` THEN
        IF       `sch 4 para 3(1) the means is one by which hard copy may be sent or supplied` `the means of sending or supplying` `the person posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information` EQUALS JUST TRUE
             AND `sch 4 para 4 the address is one to which hard copy may be sent or supplied` `the address is specified by the company for the purpose` `s 86 the company has its registered office at the address` `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied to the address` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is validly sent or supplied to a company if it is sent or supplied in hard copy form in accordance with this Part of this Schedule" (an unmet "if"; marginal reading (a))
    WHEN `sch 4 electronic form` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is sent or supplied in hard copy form"
    WHEN `sch 4 neither hard copy form nor electronic form` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "if it is sent or supplied in hard copy form"

