    CONSIDER `the form of the document or information`
    WHEN `sch 4 neither hard copy form nor electronic form` THEN
        IF `the form or manner has been agreed by the company`
        THEN JUST TRUE
        ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "is validly sent or supplied if it is sent or supplied in a form or manner that has been agreed by the company" (an unmet "if"; marginal reading (a))
    WHEN `sch 4 hard copy form` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "otherwise than in hard copy form or electronic form"
    WHEN `sch 4 electronic form` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "otherwise than in hard copy form or electronic form"

§§ `The Schedule as a whole: is the document or information validly sent or supplied to the company`

-- Routes the answer through para 1 (does the Schedule apply), then Part 2 (hard copy), Part 2A (registrar or Secretary of State),
-- Part 3 (electronic form, other senders) and Part 4 (neither). Each limb is the paragraph's own function above; nothing is restated.
-- This is a composition for the seat layer: it claims no more than the paragraphs it calls (a NOTHING from any limb that does not
-- reach the facts stays NOTHING).
-- src:19397 | 1 (1) This Schedule applies to documents or information sent or supplied to a company.
-- src:19398 | (2) It does not apply to documents or information sent or supplied by another company (see section 1144(3) and Schedule 5).
@ref sch 4 paras 1, 2, 4A, 5 and 8 Validly sent or supplied to a company (src:19397-19398)
GIVEN `the document or information is sent or supplied to a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document or information is sent or supplied by another company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the sender is the registrar or the Secretary of State` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form of the document or information` IS A `sch 4 form of the document or information`
      `the means of sending or supplying` IS A `sch 4 means of sending or supplying`
      `the person posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is registered under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address is the company's registered email address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address is specified by the company for that purpose (generally or specifically)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has agreed (generally or specifically) that the document or information may be sent or supplied in electronic form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has revoked that agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company is deemed to have agreed by a provision in the Companies Acts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address is specified for the purpose by the company (generally or specifically)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address is deemed by a provision in the Companies Acts to have been so specified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the address is specified by the company for the purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 86 the company has its registered office at the address` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied to the address` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the form or manner has been agreed by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`sch 4 the document or information is validly sent or supplied to the company` MEANS
    CONSIDER `sch 4 para 1 this Schedule applies to the document or information` `the document or information is sent or supplied to a company` `the document or information is sent or supplied by another company`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN `the answer by the paragraph that fits`
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): this Schedule applies only to "documents or information sent or supplied to a company" other than by another company
    WHERE
        `the answer by the paragraph that fits` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the form of the document or information`
            WHEN `sch 4 hard copy form` THEN
                `sch 4 para 2 the document or information is validly sent or supplied in hard copy form` `the form of the document or information` `the means of sending or supplying` `the person posts a prepaid envelope containing the document or information` `the address is specified by the company for the purpose` `s 86 the company has its registered office at the address` `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied to the address`
            WHEN `sch 4 electronic form` THEN
                IF `the sender is the registrar or the Secretary of State`
                THEN `sch 4 para 4A(1) the document or information is validly sent or supplied by the registrar or the Secretary of State in electronic form` `the sender is the registrar or the Secretary of State` `the form of the document or information` `the means of sending or supplying` `the company is registered under this Act` `the address is the company's registered email address` `the address is specified by the company for that purpose (generally or specifically)` `the address is specified by the company for the purpose` `s 86 the company has its registered office at the address` `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied to the address`
                ELSE `sch 4 para 5 the document or information is validly sent or supplied in electronic form by a person other than the registrar or the Secretary of State` `the sender is the registrar or the Secretary of State` `the form of the document or information` `the means of sending or supplying` `the company has agreed (generally or specifically) that the document or information may be sent or supplied in electronic form` `the company has revoked that agreement` `the company is deemed to have agreed by a provision in the Companies Acts` `the address is specified for the purpose by the company (generally or specifically)` `the address is deemed by a provision in the Companies Acts to have been so specified` `the address is specified by the company for the purpose` `s 86 the company has its registered office at the address` `a provision of the Companies Acts authorises the document or information to be sent or supplied to the address`
            WHEN `sch 4 neither hard copy form nor electronic form` THEN
                `sch 4 para 8 the document or information is validly sent or supplied in another agreed form or manner` `the form of the document or information` `the form or manner has been agreed by the company`
